The "infinite gold bug", requiring at least 1 zorkmid, sounds like it may
be the same one that has been around (at least on UNIX and IBM machines)
since Hack v1.  It is not so much a bug as an overlooked property of 
the way computers represent numbers.  It is definitely not a spoiler, in the
sense that it has nothing to do with the "laws of nature" in the nethack
world, i.e., nothing to do with nethack as opposed to any other program.

It is not better known because the early hack players who knew about it
considered it basically uninteresting.  It can be annoying if everyone
on a system tries it and fills up the high score list with huge bogus
scores.  For this reason I won't post it, but the curious may inquire via
email.

